============================================================
1. SECURITY GOALS
============================================================
- Protect member and officer data
- Enforce role-based access control (RBAC)
- Prevent unauthorized changes to council content
- Ensure integrity of voting and financial data
- Secure authentication and session handling
- Provide auditability for all admin actions


============================================================
2. AUTHENTICATION MODEL
============================================================

AUTH METHOD
-----------
- Email + password
- Passwords hashed with strong algorithm (e.g., bcrypt/argon2)
- No plaintext passwords stored

SESSION / TOKENS
----------------
- JWT access tokens
- Stored in httpOnly, secure cookies
- Short-lived access tokens (e.g., 15–30 minutes)
- Optional refresh tokens with rotation

LOGIN FLOW
----------
1. User submits email + password to /auth/login
2. Backend verifies credentials
3. Backend issues JWT with:
   - user_id
   - roles (e.g., ["member", "grand_knight"])
   - expiry
4. JWT stored in httpOnly cookie
5. Frontend reads auth state via /auth/me


============================================================
3. AUTHORIZATION MODEL (RBAC)
============================================================

ROLE STORAGE
------------
- roles table
- user_roles join table
- Roles embedded in JWT

ROLE ENFORCEMENT (BACKEND)
--------------------------
- FastAPI dependency checks JWT
- Extract roles from token
- Route-level decorators enforce required roles
  - @requires_roles("admin")
  - @requires_roles("grand_knight", "webmaster")

ROLE ENFORCEMENT (FRONTEND)
---------------------------
- AuthContext stores user + roles
- <AuthGuard> ensures user is logged in
- <RoleGuard roles={['admin', 'grand_knight']}> wraps admin pages
- Menus and buttons hidden if role not present

DATA-LEVEL AUTHORIZATION
------------------------
- Member-specific data filtered by user_id
- Admin actions restricted by role:
  - FS/Treasurer: finance
  - GK/DGK: governance
  - Webmaster: technical settings
- Voting: one vote per user per vote_id (enforced by UNIQUE constraint)


============================================================
4. INPUT VALIDATION & SANITIZATION
============================================================

BACKEND VALIDATION
------------------
- All request bodies validated via Pydantic schemas
- Type checking, length limits, enum validation
- Reject malformed or unexpected fields

FRONTEND VALIDATION
-------------------
- Basic validation for UX (required fields, formats)
- Never rely solely on frontend validation

SANITIZATION
------------
- HTML inputs sanitized server-side
- Prevent XSS in:
  - News content
  - Recognition descriptions
  - Program descriptions
  - Prayer requests

FILE UPLOADS
------------
- Limit file size (e.g., 10–50 MB)
- Restrict file types (images, PDFs)
- Store files outside web root or behind authenticated endpoints
- Generate safe filenames


============================================================
5. TRANSPORT & STORAGE SECURITY
============================================================

TRANSPORT
---------
- All traffic over HTTPS
- TLS termination at ingress (K3s)
- HSTS enabled

STORAGE
-------
- Passwords hashed (bcrypt/argon2)
- Secrets (DB passwords, JWT keys) stored in:
  - Kubernetes secrets
  - Sealed-secrets for GitOps
- No secrets in source control

DATABASE
--------
- Principle of least privilege for DB user
- Separate DB users for app, migrations, and reporting
- Regular backups with encrypted storage


============================================================
6. VOTING & FINANCIAL DATA INTEGRITY
============================================================

VOTING
------
- vote_cast table enforces UNIQUE (vote_id, user_id)
- All voting actions logged in audit_log
- Voting endpoints require member/admin roles
- No client-side only enforcement; backend always checks

FINANCIAL
---------
- Dues and budget changes restricted to FS/Treasurer/GK
- All financial changes logged in audit_log
- No direct SQL from frontend; only via validated APIs


============================================================
7. AUDIT LOGGING & MONITORING
============================================================

AUDIT LOG
---------
- audit_log table:
  - user_id
  - action
  - details
  - created_at
- Log all admin actions:
  - Content changes
  - Member updates
  - Financial changes
  - Voting configuration changes
  - Role changes

APPLICATION LOGGING
-------------------
- Structured JSON logs
- Include request_id and user_id when available
- Log errors with stack traces (internal only)

MONITORING
----------
- Health checks for API, workers, DB
- Metrics for:
  - Login failures
  - 4xx/5xx rates
  - Task failures (Celery)
- Alerts for unusual activity


============================================================
8. FRONTEND SECURITY
============================================================

XSS PROTECTION
--------------
- Escape all dynamic content in React
- Use dangerouslySetInnerHTML only with sanitized content
- No inline event handlers with untrusted data

CSRF PROTECTION
---------------
- Use same-site cookies (LAX/STRICT) for JWT
- For sensitive endpoints, consider CSRF tokens if needed

CLICKJACKING
------------
- Set X-Frame-Options: DENY
- Or Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors 'none'


============================================================
9. CELERY & BACKGROUND TASK SECURITY
============================================================

TASK SECURITY
-------------
- Tasks must validate inputs
- Tasks must not trust client-provided IDs blindly
- Tasks must run under least-privilege DB user

QUEUE ISOLATION
---------------
- Separate queues for:
  - email_queue
  - media_queue
  - voting_queue
  - audit_queue

RETRY & FAILURE
---------------
- Retry with backoff for transient errors
- Log failures with context
- No silent failures


============================================================
10. DEPLOYMENT & ENVIRONMENT SECURITY
============================================================

K3s CLUSTER
-----------
- Namespaces per environment (prod, staging)
- Network policies to restrict pod communication
- Ingress only for public-facing services

HELM & CONFIG
-------------
- values.yaml for non-secret config
- Secrets via Kubernetes secrets / sealed-secrets
- No hardcoded secrets in charts

ENVIRONMENTS
------------
- Separate staging and production
- No test data in production
- No production data in staging


============================================================
11. SECURITY REVIEW & MAINTENANCE
============================================================

REGULAR REVIEWS
---------------
- Review roles & permissions annually
- Review audit logs regularly
- Review DB indexes and constraints

PATCHING
--------
- Keep dependencies updated:
  - React
  - FastAPI
  - Postgres
  - Redis
  - Celery
- Apply security patches promptly

INCIDENT RESPONSE
-----------------
- Define process for:
  - Breach detection
  - Containment
  - Notification
  - Recovery
